+# concerns.md format
+
+`docs/concerns.md` is align's artifact for **unresolved pressure** — not delivery sequencing, not
+decisions.
+
+## Order and numbers
+
+- File order is **priority**, highest first: how much it blocks the current build, and how hard it
+  is to absorb later.
+- Heading is `## N. Title`. **N is a stable ID, not a rank.** Reordering to match priority does not
+  change N.
+- A settled concern moves out to its owning ADR or architecture section and **leaves a gap**. Never
+  renumber. Never resolve in place.
+- `## Accepted residual risks` (and similar trailers) are not numbered concerns.
+
+## Entry
+
+```md
+## N. Title
+
+**Kind:** {sort of pressure, and whether a driver exists} · **Refs:** {ADRs, architecture sections, sibling concerns}
+
+{the pressure}
+
+→ queued as <ticket-slug>
+```
+
+The queued line is optional. When a concern is queued as work, keep only the architectural contact
+surface plus that line; the deliberation moves into the ticket.
+
+Cite by slug (`concerns.md#n-title-slug`) or by ID (`concern 4`). Do not cite by file position.

