### to-tickets/NOTION-FORMAT.md [missing]
--- M/to-tickets/NOTION-FORMAT.md
+++ A/to-tickets/NOTION-FORMAT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
+# Notion entry format
+
+Project-local, divergent by design. Why the board exists, where it is pinned and how it is queried are
+[the development process](../../docs/process.md#the-seam)'s. This shelf holds what a pass writes onto an
+entry, and when.
+
+Every ticket has an entry, whether or not the work earns a document here.
+
+## The entry explains itself
+
+An entry is read on the board before anything else, so it stands alone. Its title says what changes for
+whoever uses the product, in words that need no file open to parse — never an implementation name. Its
+body is a short paragraph or two: what the work delivers, and for a fix, the symptom it removes. Neither
+restates the document here, and neither substitutes for one.
+
+An entry a pass creates carries 🤖 as its icon, so the board shows at a glance what an agent wrote and
+what a person did. Report its URL in the session — an entry nobody can reach is an entry nobody reviews.
+
+## The properties
+
+The board holds `Status`, `Priority`, `Effort`, `Driver`, `Objective`, `Type`, `Interaction`,
+`Initiative`, `Team`, `Assignee`, `Requested by`, the parent and sub-ticket relations, and `Ticket` — the
+URL of the document here, when one exists. `Blocked By` and `Is Blocking` are left alone: a dependency is
+argued rather than queried, so it lives in the document as `Depends on` and nowhere else.
+
+A pass sets `Status`, `Effort`, `Type`, `Interaction`, `Team`, `Assignee` and `Ticket` whenever they
+change. It sets `Priority` and `Driver` once at inception and never revises them, because reprioritising
+is a human act. `Sprint` is not maintained and no pass sets it; `Component` is unused.
+
+`Objective`, `Initiative` and `Requested by` are set at inception too, from the context that produced the
+ticket or by asking. They are never left empty and never guessed: `Initiative` carries the roadmap's
+rollups, so a ticket without one is invisible to it. Where a sibling or parent is already classified,
+follow it rather than reasoning from the option name. `Requested by` names the customer whose report
+produced the work, and takes a new option when that customer has none.
+
+`Type` names what the work is: `Improvement`, `Issue`, `Data`, `Verification`, and `Maintenance` for work
+that keeps what exists working. Choose `Maintenance`; the `Tech Debt` option remains only on tickets not
+yet re-tagged.
+
+`Interaction` is `HITL` or `AFK` → [the slicing rules](./SKILL.md).
+
+`Effort` — `Minimal Effort`, `Hour Of Craft`, `Day of Craft`, `Week of Craft`, `Undisentangled` — says
+where to look rather than deciding. Whether the work earns a document here is
+[the process](../../docs/process.md#the-ticket)'s.
+
+`Team` is `Development` on everything here, and every ticket is assigned to Fima for as long as he is the
+only developer.
+
+A pass does not add an option to any property. The vocabularies are decided, and a pass that invents a
+value hides work rather than classifying it, so an option is added only on explicit instruction. The
+exception is `Requested by`, where a customer with no option yet gets one.
+
+## Status
+
+`Not Started` → `In Progress` → `Next Release` → `Done`. A pass sets the first three. `Next Release`
+means merged and waiting on a production release, which is the last state this side can observe; the
+column empties at each release rather than accumulating, because `Done` is set by hand once the release
+ships.
+
+`Superseded` closes a ticket folded into another or replaced by one. `Paused` is held by older tickets.
+`QA Aproval` and `On-hold` are unused, and no pass sets them.
+
+Minting is not the only pass that needs this file: whichever pass changes reality moves `Status` with it.

